b.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99030","id":2467709295,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TFkFv","user":{"login":"tracefree","id":155747722,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUiFig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155747722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree","html_url":"https://github.com/tracefree","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T09:56:42Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T12:33:06Z","body":"I think this may be a side effect of the logic used to ensure the radius is scaled only uniformly by the value of the largest global scale axis, but you are right that it feels strange and I'll take a look to see if that really is the case or if there is a coding mistake.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2467709295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468015317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99030#issuecomment-2468015317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99030","id":2468015317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TGuzV","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T12:05:01Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T12:05:01Z","body":"I guess it is just the usual flaw with the Transform2D that has no real scale compare to 3D but just a rotation depending fake scale.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468015317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468956678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99030#issuecomment-2468956678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99030","id":2468956678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKUoG","user":{"login":"tracefree","id":155747722,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUiFig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155747722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree","html_url":"https://github.com/tracefree","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:19:05Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T20:21:52Z","body":"Yeah, it looks like that's what's happening here. For the scale factor of the radius, I take the largest value of the `global_scale` of the obstacle node, clamped to 0.0001 to prevent it from becoming zero or negative.\r\n\r\nHow would you like me to handle this? I don't really see another sensible way of using the transform's scale to influence the radius, but the fact that it depends on the rotation is very counter-intuitive and I imagine would lead several people to report it as a bug. Do we leave it as is, or should we maybe just leave the radius alone and let it ignore the node transform? And if the latter, should I change the 3D PR to do it like that as well for consistency?\r\n\r\nIf we stay with the current behavior I could change the warning that is already displayed when scaling a radius-based obstacle non-uniformly to also warn about unexpected behavior. Currently it just says \"The agent radius can only be scaled uniformly. The largest scale value along the two axes will be used and skew is ignored.\"","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468956678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":n